---
import LegalDocument from '@/components/legal/legal-document.astro';
import PageIntro from '@/components/page-intro.astro';
import SubpageLayout from '@/layouts/subpage-layout.astro';

const toc = [
  { id: 'using-groam', title: 'Using Groam' },
  { id: 'your-account', title: 'Your account' },
  { id: 'your-content', title: 'Your content' },
  { id: 'groups', title: 'Groups and shared trips' },
  { id: 'ai', title: 'AI agents' },
  { id: 'pricing', title: 'Pricing' },
  { id: 'acceptable-use', title: 'Acceptable use' },
  { id: 'availability', title: 'Availability and liability' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes to these terms' }
];
---

<SubpageLayout
  title="Terms"
  description="The agreement between you and Groam when you use it to plan trips."
>
  <PageIntro
    title="Terms"
    lede="The agreement between you and Groam when you use it to plan trips with your group."
  />
  <LegalDocument toc={toc} updated="17 October 2026">
    <section id="using-groam">
      <h2>Using Groam</h2>
      <p>
        Groam is a place to plan trips with a group: a shared itinerary, ideas, issues, and
        conversations. By creating an account or using Groam you agree to these terms. If you
        do not agree, please do not use it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="your-account">
      <h2>Your account</h2>
      <p>
        You are responsible for what happens under your account. Keep your sign-in details
        safe, and tell us if you think someone else has access.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="your-content">
      <h2>Your content</h2>
      <p>
        Your trips, ideas, issues, messages, and files stay yours. You give Groam permission
        to store and display them as needed to run the product for you and your group. You
        confirm that you have the right to add what you add.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="groups">
      <h2>Groups and shared trips</h2>
      <p>
        Trips live in groups. Members can see, suggest changes to, and discuss a group's
        trips, and every change is recorded with its author. Think about what you share
        before you add it to a group you do not control.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="ai">
      <h2>AI agents</h2>
      <p>
        Groam's AI agents run on your own connected ChatGPT account, under that service's
        terms. Agents can make mistakes. Check what they suggest, especially bookings, times,
        and costs, before you rely on it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="pricing">
      <h2>Pricing</h2>
      <p>
        Planning on your own is free. Inviting travelers will cost €1 per invited traveler,
        once. Paid invites are not live yet, and these terms will be updated with the details
        before they are.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="acceptable-use">
      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Do not break the law or use Groam to harm other people.</li>
        <li>Do not try to get into accounts, trips, or systems that are not yours.</li>
        <li>Do not disrupt the service or misuse it at a scale that affects others.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="availability">
      <h2>Availability and liability</h2>
      <p>
        We work to keep Groam running and your plans safe, but we cannot promise it will
        always be available or free of errors. Groam helps you organize a trip; the decisions
        and bookings you make from it are yours. To the extent the law allows, Groam is
        provided as is.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="changes">
      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        This is a draft. If we change it in a way that matters, we will update the date at the
        top of the page. Continuing to use Groam after a change means you accept it.
      </p>
    </section>
  </LegalDocument>
</SubpageLayout>
